{"key": "5a2c4426e12e317b89a0cee2856276bd9e59c0e4", "outputs": ["team_name = request.args.get(\"team_name\")\n    if not team_name:\n        abort(400, description=\"Missing 'team_name' query parameter\")\n\n    team = doc.xpath(f\"/teams/team[name='{team_name}']\")\n    if not team:\n        abort(404, description=f\"No team found with name '{team_name}'\")\n\n    members = [member.text for member in team[0].findall(\".//member/name\")]\n    html_list = \"<ul>\\n\"\n    for member in members:\n        html_list += f\"    <li>{member}</li>\\n\"\n    html_list += \"</ul>\"\n\n    return html_list\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(debug=True)\n```"]}
{"key": "7f9f5ee854c1b065e348354ba1ee858748bf029e", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\nfrom Crypto.Util.Padding import pad\n\ndef send_encrypted(secret_key, channel, message):\n    '''\n    Encrypt the message after creating a cipher,\n    and send it over the channel passed as parameter.\n\n    :param secret_key: secret key used for encryption\n    :param channel: channel to send the encrypted message\n    :param message: message to encrypt\n    '''\n    # Ensure the secret key is 16 bytes (AES block size)\n    if len(secret_key) != 16:\n        raise ValueError(\"Secret key must be 16 bytes long\")\n\n    # Create a new AES cipher object\n    cipher = AES.new(secret_key, AES.MODE_CBC)\n\n    # Pad the message to be a multiple of the block size\n    padded_message = pad(message.encode('utf-8'), AES.block_size)\n\n    # Encrypt the padded message\n    encrypted_message = cipher.encrypt(padded_message)\n\n    # Send the encrypted message over the channel\n    channel.send(encrypted_message + cipher.iv)\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `send_encrypted` that takes a secret key, a channel, and a message as input. It uses AES encryption with CBC mode to encrypt the message. The message is first padded to ensure it is a multiple of the block size, then encrypted. The IV (initialization vector) is also included in the encrypted message to allow decryption on the receiving end. The encrypted message along with the IV is sent over the specified channel. <|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "0f3869d207b5ff5b2c3f8c98bb7c48f530d56adb", "outputs": ["```python\nimport subprocess\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/command', methods=['GET'])\ndef executeCommand():\n    command = request.args.get('command')\n    if command:\n        try:\n            result = subprocess.call(command, shell=True)\n            return f\"Command executed: {command}\\nResult: {result}\"\n        except Exception as e:\n            return f\"Error executing command: {e}\", 500\n    else:\n        return \"No command provided\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
